      "description": "Watch Norway vs Denmark highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 24, 2026. Haaland's Late Strike Seals Thrilling Victory for Norway Against Denmark A match of twists and turns and intense emotions marked the clash between Norway and Denmark, with the decisive goal arriving in the dying moments. A Fiery Start to the Encounter The game, played on September 24, 2026, kicked off with a high tempo. Norway managed to break the deadlock in the 14th minute through Oscar Bobb , assisted by Martin Oedegaard . However, Denmark responded swiftly. After a VAR check, their first goal was validated, with Erling Haaland finding the net in the 18th minute, following a pass from Antonio Nusa . Despite this setback, the Danish side showed resilience. In the 25th minute, Mikkel Damsgaard reduced the deficit with a spectacular direct free-kick, bringing Denmark firmly back into contention. A Second Half of High Drama The second half brought even more drama. Denmark managed to restore parity in the 60th minute when Rasmus Hoejlund headed home. The Danish jubilation, however, was short-lived. Norway , driven by their attack, found the net once more. In the 74th minute, Erling Haaland scored his second of the match, following a move initiated by Antonio Nusa and with Martin Oedegaard providing the assist, putting Norway back in front. A Tense Finale The closing stages of the match became increasingly physical with numerous interruptions. Denmark pushed for an equalizer, but Norway held firm to their lead. Both teams saw players receive yellow cards, and David Moeller Wolfe of Norway was sent off for a second yellow following a foul on Gustav Isaksen in injury time. Despite Denmark's late efforts, the scoreline held, with Norway emerging victorious from a memorable encounter. Match Details Possession was nearly evenly split, with Norway holding 52% and Denmark 48% by the final whistle. The attendance at the stadium was 25,002."
